# The images' build context is the repository root (apps/*/Dockerfile). Send only what a build
# reads: never this machine's dependencies, builds, caches or secrets. A file listed here also
# cannot invalidate the layers that copy the sources. Keep it in step with .gitignore, and keep
# every workspace package's package.json (the frozen install needs them all).

# Dependencies and builds: the image installs and builds its own.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.output
**/.nitro
**/.tanstack
**/.vite
**/out-tsc
**/coverage
**/test-output
**/tmp
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/api/migrations

# Secrets: only .env.example is committed.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Git, Nx's cache, agents' worktrees and local files, and what no build reads. Not all of
# .agents: Nx evaluates every project's configs, and eslint.config.mjs reads
# .agents/generated.json.
.git
.nx
.claude
.agents/*
!.agents/generated.json
.github
.playwright-cli
docs
**/*.md
# `pnpm pw:agents` (opt-in, per machine): the planner's test plans and the .mcp.json it writes
/specs/
/.mcp.json

# The image definitions: editing one must not invalidate the copied sources.
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
